                        "entry_id": "432b4947-5166-3029-8dc0-70e970d3494d",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Empetrum nigrum, a species of crowberry."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "bf558fe7-504a-4aaa-bbff-0a1913726b90",
                                "sense_id": "632298ee-e348-30c1-92be-9ac3cf488f70",
                                "text": "Many kinds of wild fruit gave variety to our diet of fish and birds—red currants and gooseberries, red raspberries and black mossberries, high and low-bush cranberries, and, best of all, the northern blueberries, which grow profusely all over this part of the Yukon."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "cbb2e791-41e4-4504-8526-c9b9533419ed",
                                "sense_id": "632298ee-e348-30c1-92be-9ac3cf488f70",
                                "text": "Small black mossberries, indigenous to the Aleutian Islands, are a favorite of the Aleuts, but almost any wild berry will do, as well as garden variety currants, cooked and sweetened cranberries, and, in Alaska, any variety of tundra fruit."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "ccc48f4e-759d-416b-9382-ccd8013b51a7",
                                "sense_id": "632298ee-e348-30c1-92be-9ac3cf488f70",
                                "text": "She saw a patch of mossberries, the shiny black berries nearly hidden in a tangle of heather, and stopped to pick them."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
